  "description": "BEWJUM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H96 Co2 Dy4 N6 O36,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.267-4.020 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.69-114.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co2Dy4(OH)2(ib)8(bdea)2(NO3)4(H2O)2]·2MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Dy(III).",
